  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "get_buffer",
    "file": "ffmpeg/libavcodec/svq3.c",
    "description": "Heap buffer overflow is caused by under-allocating the edge emulation scratch buffer. get_buffer() allocates s->edge_emu_buffer as av_calloc(pic->f->linesize[0], 17), but svq3_mc_dir_part() calls vdsp.emulated_edge_mc() with block sizes up to (width+1,height+1) for luma and chroma, and ff_emulated_edge_mc_8 writes up to block_w bytes per row across block_h rows. For this PoV, the allocated 17*linesize region is too small for a requested emulated block, and ff_emulated_edge_mc_8 performs a 1-byte write past the end (videodsp_template.c:101). Crash site is ff_emulated_edge_mc_8, but root cause is incorrect buffer sizing in svq3 get_buffer().",
    "conditions": "In SVQ3 decoding, a frame/macroblock must take the motion-compensation edge-emulation path (emu=1 in svq3_mc_dir_part, i.e., MV near/outside frame edge). Then svq3_mc_dir_part invokes emulated_edge_mc on s->edge_emu_buffer for luma/chroma with dimensions derived from partition size (+1). With crafted bitstream values (as in the provided PoV), required temporary edge block exceeds 17*linesize bytes allocated in get_buffer(), leading to out-of-bounds write in ff_emulated_edge_mc_8 during right-edge fill."
  },
